an for meeting the resident's most immediate needs within 48 hours of being admitted","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0657":{"code":"F-0657","title":"Develop the complete care plan within 7 days of the comprehensive assessment; and prepared, reviewed, and revised by a team of health professionals.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0690":{"code":"F-0690","title":"Provide appropriate care for residents who are continent or incontinent of bowel/bladder, appropriate catheter care,  and appropriate care  to prevent urinary tract infections.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0759":{"code":"F-0759","title":"Ensure medication error rates are not 5 percent or greater.","category":"Pharmacy Service Deficiencies","concept":"medication","concept_label":"Medication management"},"cms-f0868":{"code":"F-0868","title":"Have the Quality Assessment and Assurance group have the required members and meet at least quarterly","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0838":{"code":"F-0838","title":"Conduct and document a facility-wide assessment to determine what resources are necessary to care for residents competently during both day-to-day operations (including nights and weekends) and emergencies.","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0842":{"code":"F-0842","title":"Safeguard resident-identifiable information and/or maintain medical records on each resident that are in accordance with accepted professional standards.","category":"Resident Assessment and Care Planning Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-k0291":{"code":"